      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-06-06_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <head>MR. W. C. ANDERSON AT WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>MR. W. C. ANDERSON AT WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>levt g Cornwall</p>
        <p>There is no better place in England for a HOLIDAY than DEVON or CORNWALL. The charming scenery of the two counties, the lovely coast line and rugged moorlands, combined with mild and equable climate, constitute a RIVIERA of which England has reason to be proud. In no other part of the United Kingdom is there such diversity of scenery and such charm of surroundings for all in search of rest, change and sunshine.</p>
        <p>Send for one or both of the high-class travel books:— "DEVON THE SHIRE OF THE SEA KINGS." and "THE CORNISH RIVIERA." These useful, beliday-planning publications are beautifully illustrated and well written. and may be obtained from the superintendent of the Line, G.W.R., Paddington Station. W. for postage 3d. each: from whom may also be obtained full particulars of the cheap week-end, excursion and tourist fares.</p>
        <p>EXPRESS SERVICES FROM ALL PARTS BY 0. W. A.</p>
        <p>WW.IRgoI</p>
      </div>
