        <head>WARRIN (flu r COUNCIL. WARRINGTON BRIDGE: .Aldernma Bannett Objects to the Girder Schwan. The monthly meeting 9f the Warrington Town Council was hold at the Town Hall on Tuesday evening under the presidency of the Mayor (Alderman Smethurst). There were also present :—The Deputy Mayor (Alderman Bolton), Aldermen A. Bennett, T. Button., L. Ellison, John Evans, W. J. Forshaw, V. Piet-point, D. Tinnion ; Councillors T. IL Ashcroft, J. Ball, T. Barton, J. Broadhurst. T. C'unntler, E. Cannington, J. Dickenson, James Evans. J. Hawthorn, J. J. Nielci, \V. B. Roberts, W. Rogers, J. Sankey, H. Singleton, J. Skelland, T. S. Steel. J. Fulton-Smith, F. Stott, 0. Toole, J. Wilkinson, W. J. Wilson, Afessrs. J. L. Whittle (town clerk), A. T. Rollaway (deputy town clerk), J. Foirburst (borough treasurer), J. Bees (water engineer), W. S. Haddock (gas engineer), F. V. L. Mathias (electrical engineer), J. M. Murray (director of education), F. G. Ruddock (borough analyst) and Dr. J. C. Hibbert (medical officer). VICTORIA PARK.</head>
        <p>WARRIN (flu r COUNCIL. WARRINGTON BRIDGE: .Aldernma Bannett Objects to the Girder Schwan. The monthly meeting 9f the Warrington Town Council was hold at the Town Hall on Tuesday evening under the presidency of the Mayor (Alderman Smethurst). There were also present :—The Deputy Mayor (Alderman Bolton), Aldermen A. Bennett, T. Button., L. Ellison, John Evans, W. J. Forshaw, V. Piet-point, D. Tinnion ; Councillors T. IL Ashcroft, J. Ball, T. Barton, J. Broadhurst. T. C'unntler, E. Canning- ton, J. Dickenson, James Evans. J. Hawthorn, J. J. Nielci, \V. B. Roberts, W. Rogers, J. Sankey, H. Single- ton, J. Skelland, T. S. Steel. J. Fulton-Smith, F. Stott, 0. Toole, J. Wilkinson, W. J. Wilson, Afessrs. J. L. Whittle (town clerk), A. T. Rollaway (deputy town clerk), J. Foirburst (borough treasurer), J. Bees (water engineer), W. S. Haddock (gas engineer), F. V. L. Mathias (electrical engineer), J. M. Murray (director of education), F. G. Ruddock (borough analyst) and Dr. J. C. Hibbert (medical officer). VICTORIA PARK.</p>
        <p>The Finance and Estate Committee considered the following resolution of the Town Hall, Parks and Baths Committee :—" Resolved, that the Finance and Estate Committee be requested to give Miss Fryer notice to quit the grazing land at Victoria Park coloure). green on the phn attached to the.agreement entered into by her, and dated the Bth of February, 1938." It was resolved, that the proposal be not entertained. Alderman Bc•svErr in moviuz the adoption of the minutes said he did not agree with the resolution as to Victoria Park. It was the greatest mistake in the world„ because the amount they got from the land was trivial and those green acres would be of infinite value to the inhabitants of Latchford. Councillor WI txrssoN seconded, Alderman BOLTON moved that the minute with refer- ence to the grazing land be referred back as he held that the Finance Committee had nothing to do with it, Alderman ELLISON seconded. He daid he had been trying to get the whole of the park thrown open and on almost every occasion a stumbling-block had been placed in the way by the Finance Committee re-letting the land. Councillor STOTT : What is the income from theland? Alderman Bourog : £5O a year. The Tows CLEnK said the Town Council a few month's ago agreed to let the land to Miss Fryer subject to three months' notice. .</p>
